solution_original:
4.Reference：HKDSE Math M2 2012 Q2
（a）$(1+k x)^{n}$
$$
\begin{align*}
& =1+n(k x)+\frac{n(n-1)(k x)^{2}}{2}+\cdots \\
& =1+n k x+\frac{n(n-1) k^{2}}{2} x^{2}+\cdots  \tag{$1 \mathrm{M}+1 \mathrm{~A}$}\\
& \therefore\left\{\begin{array}{l}
n k=-24 \ldots \ldots \ldots \ldots \ldots \ldots(1) \\
\frac{n(n-1) k^{2}}{2}=252 \ldots \ldots(2)
\end{array}\right. \tag{1 M}
\end{align*}
$$
From（1）,$k=-\frac{24}{n}$
Substituting（3）into（2）,
$$
\begin{align*}
\frac{n(n-1)}{2} \times\left(-\frac{24}{n}\right)^{2} & =252 \\
576 n^{2}-576 n & =504 n^{2} \\
72 n(n-8) & =0 \\
n & =\underline{\underline{8}} \text { or } 0 \text { (rejected) } \tag{1A}
\end{align*}
$$
Substituting $n=8$ into（3）,
$$
\begin{align*}
k & =-\frac{24}{8} \\
& =\underline{\underline{-3}} \tag{1A}
\end{align*}
$$
(b) Coefficient of $x^{3}=C_{3}^{8}(-3)^{3}$
$$
\begin{equation*}
=\underline{\underline{-1512}} \tag{1A}
\end{equation*}
$$

