3. Reference：HKDSE Math M2 2013 Q2
$$
(1+a x)^{n}
$$
$$
\begin{align*}
& =1+C_{1}^{n}(a x)+C_{2}^{n}(a x)^{2}+C_{3}^{n}(a x)^{3}+\cdots \\
& =1+n a x+\frac{n(n-1) a^{2}}{2} x^{2}+\frac{n(n-1)(n-2) a^{3}}{6} x^{3}+\cdots \\
& \therefore\left\{\begin{array}{l}
n a=-16 \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \\
\frac{n(n-1) a^{2}}{2}+\frac{n(n-1)(n-2) a^{3}}{6}=-336 \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots \cdots
\end{array}\right. \tag{1}
\end{align*}
$$
From（1）：$a=-\frac{16}{n}$
Substituting（3）into（2）,
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{128 n(n-1)}{n^{2}}-\frac{2048 n(n-1)(n-2)}{3 n^{3}} & =-336 \\
384 n^{2}(n-1)-2048 n(n-1)(n-2) & =-1008 n^{3} \\
-656 n^{3}+5760 n^{2}-4096 n & =0 \\
-16 n(n-8)(41 n-32) & =0
\end{aligned}
$$
Since $n$ is a positive integer,$n=8$ . Substituting $n=8$ into（3）,
$$
\begin{aligned}
a & =-\frac{16}{8} \\
& =\underline{\underline{-2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

