question_text_original:
Let $n$ be a positive integer.

1. Define $M=\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$. Evaluate
   1. $M^2$;
   2. $M^n$;
   3. $\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\2&1\end{pmatrix}^n$.
2. Evaluate
   1. $\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{n}2^k$;
   2. $\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\0&2\end{pmatrix}^n$.

