Reference：HKDSE Math M2 SP Q6
Differentiating both sides of the equation with respect to $x$ ,we have
$$
\begin{align*}
8 e^{x+y}\left(1+\frac{d y}{d x}\right) & =2 x+2 y \frac{d y}{d x} \\
4 e^{x+y}+4 e^{x+y} \frac{d y}{d x} & =x+y \frac{d y}{d x} \\
\left(4 e^{x+y}-y\right) \frac{d y}{d x} & =x-4 e^{x+y} \\
\frac{d y}{d x} & =\frac{x-4 e^{x+y}}{4 e^{x+y}-y} \tag{1A}
\end{align*}
$$
Slope of the tangent at $C$
$$
\begin{align*}
& =\left.\frac{d y}{d x}\right|_{(2,-2)} \\
& =\frac{2-4 e^{2-2}}{4 e^{2-2}-(-2)} \\
& =-\frac{1}{3} \tag{1A}
\end{align*}
$$
The equation of the tangent is
$$
\begin{align*}
y-(-2) & =-\frac{1}{3}(x-2)  \tag{1M}\\
x+3 y+4 & =0 \tag{1A}
\end{align*}
$$

