& =\frac{\pi}{4}\left(h^{2}+2 h+1\right) \frac{d h}{d t}
\end{aligned}
$$
1A
Since water leaks out at a constant rate of $\pi \mathrm{cm}^{3} \mathrm{~s}^{-1}, \frac{d V}{d t}=-\pi$ .
When $h=3$ ,
$$
\begin{aligned}
-\pi & =\left.\frac{\pi}{4}\left[3^{2}+2(3)+1\right] \frac{d h}{d t}\right|_{h=3} \\
\left.\frac{d h}{d t}\right|_{h=3} & =-\frac{1}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$
$\therefore \quad$ The rate of change of water level is $-\frac{1}{4} \mathrm{~cm} \mathrm{~s}^{-1}$ .
1M
